meta {
  name: Print Labels (Multiple)
  type: http
  seq: 39
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/accession/order-samples/print-labels
  body: json
  auth: bearer
}

headers {
  content-type: application/json
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{businessAccessToken}}
}

body:json {
  {
    "ids": ["{{sampleId}}"],
    "templateId": "{{pdfReportTemplateId}}"
  }
}

docs {
  Render many accession samples' barcode labels into ONE PDF
  (`multiple_order_label_print`), streamed back as `application/pdf`. Each sample
  becomes a row in a single `{{#each labels}}` section (barcode text, patient,
  order code, accession no, sample type, tests). The caller's `ids` order is
  preserved; unknown ids are skipped.

  ## Body
  - `ids` (required, non-empty) — accession sample ids to label.
  - `templateId` (optional) — the `multiple_order_label_print` template to render
    with. Omit to fall back to the tenant's single active multi-label template.

  ## Errors
  - 404 `ACCESSION_SAMPLE_NOT_FOUND` — none of the `ids` resolve.
  - 404 `NO_ACTIVE_LABEL_TEMPLATE` / 409 `AMBIGUOUS_LABEL_TEMPLATE` — template
    resolution failed and no `templateId` supplied.

  In Bruno, use "Save Response → Save to file" to inspect the PDF.
}
